# =============================================================================
# GEPER / kim_pipeline / bridge — code-only repository.
#
# Every path excluded below is re-created automatically on first run by
# this project's own bootstrap/download logic (verified against the
# actual loader code, not assumed) -- see DATA_PROVENANCE.md for the
# full file-by-file audit of what used to be committed here and where
# each thing actually comes from.
# =============================================================================

# --- Python ------------------------------------------------------------------
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
*$py.class
*.egg-info/
.pytest_cache/
.mypy_cache/
.ruff_cache/

# --- AI model weights / reference data (auto-downloaded on first use) -------
# See geper/pipeline/models/*/loader.py (or equivalent) for each
# plugin's real fetch source: hyena-dna clones HazyResearch/hyena-dna
# from GitHub; SPiP downloads from its own GitHub raw + SourceForge
# hosts; Enformer/Borzoi/SpliceBERT/SpliceFormer each have their own
# HuggingFace/checkpoint-URL bootstrap (see DATA_PROVENANCE.md).
geper/plugin_model_cache/
plugin_model_cache/
geper/hyena-dna/
geper/checkpoints/

# --- Evidence-source local datasets / bulk downloads (auto-bootstrapped) ----
# ClinGen, HPO, Orphanet, AlphaMissense catalogue, gnomAD, BLAST
# databases -- all self-fetch via their own pipeline/*/bootstrap.py (or
# equivalent) on first use; nothing here is meant to be committed.
geper/model_cache/
model_cache/

# --- Test cache / compiled databases -----------------------------------------
*.sqlite
*.db

# --- Run output / logs --------------------------------------------------------
geper/geper_output/
geper/logs/
*.log

# --- Offline-evidence fixture staging (geper/tests/fixtures/offline_evidence) -
# Raw geper_results.json dropped here temporarily to run extract_fixture.py
# against -- only the extracted *_evidence.json this script produces is
# meant to be committed. See that directory's README.md.
geper/tests/fixtures/offline_evidence/raw_*.json

# --- Small, checked-in test fixtures are intentionally NOT excluded here ----
# geper/testdata/, geper/testdata_bench/, test_data/ are tiny
# (low hundreds of KB combined), purpose-built fixture files (a
# generate_test_dataset.py script + small trimmed real-data slices),
# not the large re-fetchable caches this file targets -- see
# DATA_PROVENANCE.md for why these were kept.

# --- OS / editor cruft ---------------------------------------------------------
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
.idea/
.vscode/
*.swp

# --- Local tool state (not project content) ---------------------------------
.claude/

# --- Secrets / local overrides (none should ever exist, but never risk it) ---
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
config.yaml
!config.yaml.example

# Test output logs
clinical_test_output.txt
phase5d_test_output.txt

# --- The offline model-cache seed: UNTRACKED BY DESIGN, NOT BY OVERSIGHT ------
# Ruled: "The 4.6 GB seed does not go in git. Too large, and it is DERIVED
# RATHER THAN AUTHORED. It needs a documented location and a rebuild
# procedure -- where it lives on this machine, and how to regenerate it if
# lost. That is a README entry, not a commit."
#
# These two lines exist so that decision is machine-readable rather than
# prose-only: an artefact untracked BY OVERSIGHT is otherwise indistinguishable
# from one that was ruled on. Location, contents, the relationship between the
# directory and the tarball, and the rebuild procedure (with its UNKNOWNs named)
# are in DOCKER.md, under "The offline model-cache seed".
model_cache_seed/
model_cache_seed.tar.gz

# --- Pre-fetched CPU-only torch wheels -------------------------------------
# THESE ARE A BUILD DEPENDENCY, NOT CLUTTER. `Dockerfile` COPYs all three by
# exact filename and pip-installs them; without them `docker build` fails at
# the COPY step with "failed to calculate checksum of ref ...: not found",
# which names no prerequisite and appears to be a broken Dockerfile.
#
# WHY THEY ARE IGNORED RATHER THAN COMMITTED: 180 MB of binary, and they are
# DERIVED rather than authored -- byte-identical to the published upstream
# artefacts (sha256 of all three verified against download.pytorch.org on
# 2026-09-10). Same reasoning as the seed above.
#
# WHY IGNORED AT ALL, GIVEN THEY WERE ALREADY UNTRACKED: `git clean -fd`
# deletes untracked files but SKIPS ignored ones, and these were protected by
# nothing. An untracked file shows as `??`, which reads as disposable junk --
# exactly what someone running `git clean` intends to remove.
#
# *** THE LIMIT, STATED SO NOBODY RELIES ON MORE THAN THIS BUYS: `git clean
# -fdx` STILL DELETES THEM. Ignoring narrows the hazard; it does not close
# it. The standing order not to run `git clean` in the shared tree is the
# actual protection. ***
#
# .dockerignore MUST NOT exclude these -- the build context needs them.
# Ignoring here and excluding there are opposite requirements on one set of
# files, and the second one would break every build.
#
# Listed by exact filename rather than `*.whl` ON PURPOSE: a blanket pattern
# would also hide the NEXT undeclared wheel, which is this same defect. If the
# pinned versions change, these three lines and the Dockerfile's COPY lines
# must change together -- see DOCKER.md, "Before you build".
torch-2.7.1+cpu-cp312-cp312-manylinux_2_28_x86_64.whl
torchvision-0.22.1+cpu-cp312-cp312-manylinux_2_28_x86_64.whl
torchaudio-2.7.1+cpu-cp312-cp312-manylinux_2_28_x86_64.whl
